{"entity": "Pioglitazone", "type": "artifact", "description": "A specific medication belonging to the thiazolidinedione class used to enhance insulin sensitivity."}
{"entity": "Multidrug and Toxin Extrusion", "type": "concept", "description": "A renal elimination transport mechanism involved in clearing metformin from the body."}
{"entity": "Thiazolidinediones", "type": "artifact", "description": "A class of oral antidiabetic medications that may cause fluid retention and heart failure when used together with insulin products like Admelog.<SEP>A class of PPAR-gamma agonist medications that enhance insulin sensitivity in adipose and muscle tissue."}
{"entity": "Gastrointestinal Side Effects", "type": "concept", "description": "Adverse effects associated with metformin hydrochloride that are mitigated through gradual dosage escalation."}
