{"entity": "Anti-Viral Medications", "type": "concept", "description": "Anti-Viral Medications are drugs that inhibit CYP3A4 and transporters, leading to increased plasma concentrations of Atorvastatin.<SEP>A class of antiviral drugs that interact with Atorvastatin Calcium, requiring dosage limits or adjustments.<SEP>A group of antiviral agents that inhibit CYP3A4 and/or drug transporters, significantly increasing atorvastatin plasma levels."}
{"entity": "Peripheral Glucose Uptake", "type": "concept", "description": "The physiological process by which peripheral tissues take up glucose from the bloodstream, which is increased by metformin to enhance insulin sensitivity."}
{"entity": "CYP3A4", "type": "naturalobject", "description": "A cytochrome P450 enzyme whose inhibition increases Atorvastatin exposure and risk of myopathy.<SEP>CYP3A4 is a liver enzyme responsible for metabolizing Atorvastatin and targeted by various drug inhibitors.<SEP>A liver metabolic enzyme involved in drug metabolism that is inhibited by certain anti-viral medications.<SEP>A cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in pharmacokinetic interactions with warfarin sodium when influenced by inhibitors or inducers.<SEP>A CYP450 isozyme involved in the metabolism of the warfarin R-enantiomer.<SEP>A metabolic enzyme responsible for metabolizing amlodipine in the body."}
