{"entity": "NSAIDs", "type": "artifact", "description": "Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory agents that can attenuate the antihypertensive effects of lisinopril and compromise renal function.<SEP>A class of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, including ibuprofen and naproxen, that increase bleeding risk when used with warfarin.<SEP>A class of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs that damage the gastrointestinal mucosa and can inhibit CYP2C9, posing high bleeding risks when combined with warfarin.<SEP>Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs that can cause gastropathy when used.<SEP>Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs that should be avoided in chronic kidney disease as they worsen kidney function and reduce ACE inhibitor efficacy.<SEP>Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs that can interact with anticoagulants to cause bleeding and contribute to acute kidney injury or hyperkalemia.<SEP>Nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, including COX-2 NSAIDs, that increase clinically relevant bleeding risk when taken with warfarin."}
